<title>USA: USDA extends potato program through Aug 27.</title>
<headline>USDA extends potato program through Aug 27.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department Monday said it extended until August 27 its program to pay potato growers who donate 1996 crop fresh Irish potatoes to charities or for livestock feed.</p>
<p>USDA launched the program to ease a glut of potatoes and said it was extending it to give potato farmers time to comply with program rules.</p>
<p>In addition, USDA said it will now pay producers for bulk shipments to charities.</p>
</text>
